    Bug 2041692 - Inject Thunderbird-specific add-on warning messages via AddonCard.setEmbedderHooks(). r=mkmelin


    Bug 2032014 moved the Add-on Manager UI helpers out of the window scope, which
    broke the previous mechanism Thunderbird used to display custom warning banners
    for suppressed Experiments and legacy/incompatible extensions on add-on cards.

    This patch switches to the new `AddonCard.setEmbedderHooks()` static method
    added in bug 2041640. The hook receives the addon and the same context the
    default `getAddonMessageInfo` does, returns Thunderbird's custom message for
    suppressed Experiments and for legacy or incompatible extensions, and
    delegates to the imported default for cases it does not handle.

    The `browser_extension_install_experiment_suppressed.js` test is re-enabled.

    Depends on D302024 (m-c)

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302038

